WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
    In Blackrock Depths the six Ironhand Guardians flank the Iron Hall
    between Magmus and the throne room and breathe Gout of Flames (spell
    15529, a fire cone, every 16s) only while Magmus is being fought:
    `instance_blackrock_depths::SetData(TYPE_IRON_HALL, ...)` calls
    `brd_ironhand_guardian::SetData(0, value)` in its NOT_STARTED and
    IN_PROGRESS cases (instance_blackrock_depths.cpp, the TYPE_IRON_HALL
    switch, about line 621). Magmus engaging sets IN_PROGRESS (flames on).
    Magmus dying sets DONE, and the DONE case only opens the throne door:
    it never switches the flames off, and a dead Magmus cannot reset to
    NOT_STARTED. The guardians therefore keep casting until the map resets.
    A party that waits or walks in the hall after the kill takes the cone
    from creatures that never enter combat, so it reads as out of combat
    while it burns. Live: a five-member party died in the hall 30 minutes
    after killing Magmus (mod-overseer#1485).

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED
    An upstream change that turns the guardians' flames off when
    TYPE_IRON_HALL becomes DONE. No upstream PR exists yet.

